Exercises and games

Some texts in History Tracers end with an exercise. This is a short activity that helps you check whether you understood the main ideas.

An exercise consists of questions with the options Yes and No. Choose the option you believe is correct and click the Check button. History Tracers will mark whether your answer is right and explain the correct one. Click the New button to clear your answers and try again.

Try it now. The exercise at the end of this page is an example.

History Tracers also offers games. Each one has its own rules, explained on the game page. You can access them through the Games menu on the sidebar. The games provide a fun way to learn through practice.

Exercises and games invite you to learn by doing. Answer the exercise and explore the Games menu to discover the interactive activities of the project.
